  "id": "Compound::DB00877 - Gene::100861540",
  "verbalization": "Sirolimus, through its mechanism of action, appears to influence the expression or activity of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in drug metabolism. The evidence suggests that Sirolimus may act as a regulator of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p through a shared pathway involving the binding of certain compounds, such as Amiodarone and Cyclophosphamide, which both bind to this enzyme. The lowest common ancestor of these interactions points to Ketone, indicating a potential metabolic or regulatory link that is central to the relationship between Sirolimus and Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p. The consistent presence of Amiodarone and Cyclophosphamide as mediators of the interaction, along with the shared pathway through Ketone, supports the notion that Sirolimus may modulate Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p via a mechanism involving these compounds. This integrated pathway highlights the role of Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p in drug metabolism and suggests that Sirolimus could influence its activity, potentially affecting drug efficacy or toxicity.",
